{"title":"1977 Canadian MO Problems/Problem 7","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1977_Canadian_MO_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A rectangular city is exactly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> blocks long and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> blocks wide (see diagram).\nA woman lives on the southwest corner of the city and works in the northeast corner. She walks \nto work each day but, on any given trip, she makes sure that her path does not include any intersection\ntwice. Show that the number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/e/1be728aed505b28aaff3aa0b23debd2ec6172a72.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(m,n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"62\" height=\"20\" /> of different paths  she can take to work satisfies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/1/a31f393b66d2ac1c2cac1fae13368e1a759312ff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(m,n)\\le 2^{mn}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"116\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/3/5e3f766b09bab3058d8a3bdd35ddbc91cbe64a1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\underbrace{ \\left. \\begin{array}{|c|c|c|c|c|c|c|c|c|c|c| }      \\hline      &amp;&amp;&amp;&amp;&amp;&amp;&amp;&amp;&amp;&amp; \\\\ \\hline      &amp;&amp;&amp;&amp;&amp;&amp;&amp;&amp;&amp;&amp; \\\\ \\hline      &amp;&amp;&amp;&amp;&amp;&amp;&amp;&amp;&amp;&amp; \\\\ \\hline      &amp;&amp;&amp;&amp;&amp;&amp;&amp;&amp;&amp;&amp; \\\\ \\hline      &amp;&amp;&amp;&amp;&amp;&amp;&amp;&amp;&amp;&amp; \\\\ \\hline      &amp;&amp;&amp;&amp;&amp;&amp;&amp;&amp;&amp;&amp; \\\\ \\hline      &amp;&amp;&amp;&amp;&amp;&amp;&amp;&amp;&amp;&amp; \\\\ \\hline \\end{array} \\right\\}n}_m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -90px\" width=\"215\" height=\"167\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1977_Canadian_MO_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The woman's path divides the grid into two regions, one containing the northwest corner, and one containing the southeast corner. Shade all the cells in the region containing the northwest corner. Thus every path corresponds to a shading of some cells of the grid. No two paths correspond to the same shading of cells (i.e. the function that maps the woman's path to a shading of cells is injective). There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/9/0d94bf17ae61af915ca64c2897477317df80c87f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{mn}$\" width=\"29\" height=\"12\" /> possible ways to shade the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/0/150c08478d63c3d2f5cc0de4222ea9183673d7ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$mn$\" width=\"26\" height=\"8\" /> cells of the grid since each cell is either shaded or unshaded, and thus the number of different paths is at most <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/9/0d94bf17ae61af915ca64c2897477317df80c87f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{mn}$\" width=\"29\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017124315\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.008 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.026 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 39/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 1875/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:13282:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017124315 and revision id 290738. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}